## report_mini.bot — fixture for `iterion report`: a short but
## representative run (agent → tool → judge, two published artifacts, a
## conditional terminal edge) so the generated report has a real
## chronology, a real artifact table and a real outcome to render.

## `summary:` is the conventional field `iterion report` lifts into its
## artifact table — the fixture uses it so the rendered report carries
## real per-node content, not just node names.
schema note:
  value: string
  summary: string

schema check:
  value: string
  summary: string
  ok: bool

agent survey:
  model: "claude-opus-4-7"
  output: note
  publish: survey_notes

tool build:
  command: "echo built"
  output: note

judge verify:
  model: "claude-opus-4-7"
  output: check
  publish: verdict

workflow report_mini:
  worktree: none
  sandbox: none
  entry: survey

  budget:
    max_iterations: 10

  survey -> build
  build -> verify
  verify -> done when ok
  verify -> fail
